|~ Every value comes apart into the set of its atoms and a shape, and
   the shape applied to the set builds the value back [D42]. The
   atoms are the values no verb takes further apart, null, booleans,
   numbers, strings, patterns, keywords, tag names and paths, each once, in the one
   order, and a value is taken apart to the end: the keys of its maps
   and the tags over its payloads are atoms as its other leaves are.
   The shape is a quote of reads into the set, `(get /n)`, and of the
   steps that build the value from what they read: a vector is the vector of
   the shapes of its elements; a map is built from the pairs of its keys
   and values by `indexBy`; a tagged value, the set, the quote and the
   doc and an error at rest among them, from its tag and its payload by
   `tag` [D13], [D19].
   `["x" [1 1] {:b :a}]` has the atoms `#[1 "x" :a :b]` and the shape
   `~([(get /1) [(get /0) (get /0)] ([[(get /3) (get /2)]] | indexBy ~(first) | map ~last)])`. The verbs
   are the language's own, and the test of the ring runs them over every
   example of the catalog and every literal of the conformance cases.
   The decisions it exists for: [D42]. ~|

:any/atomKinds
  |~~ The kinds of the atoms, a word, since a recipe reads no value a
      sentence names.
  ~~|
  ~(#[::null ::boolean ::number ::string ::regex ::keyword ::tag ::path])

:any/groupBefore
  |~~ The step followed by the steps of the suffix, as a group, or the
      step alone under an empty suffix.
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :suffix |~~ The steps that follow the step. ~~| /0 ::vec
    | throws :suffix/NotVecError |~~ The suffix is a vector of steps. ~~|
    | impl ~(if (suffix | count | eq 0) ~() ~([[it] suffix] | flat | tag ::quote | tag ::group))

:any/partsOf
  |~~ The parts a value that is no atom is built from, and the steps
      that build it from them: a vector from its elements by none, a map
      from the pairs of its keys and values, and a tagged value, a doc
      and an error at rest among them, from its tag and its payload.
  ~~|
  ~(:kind (type)
    | cond
        ~(kind | eq ::vec) ~({:parts it :glue ~()})
        ~(kind | eq ::map) ~(:whole it | {:parts (keys | sort | map ~(:key it | [key (whole | query key)])) :glue ~(indexBy ~(first) | map ~last)})
        ~({:parts [kind (payload)] :glue ~(tag)}))

:any/atomsOf
  |~~ The atoms of a value, its own when it is an atom and otherwise
      those of its parts, each part's gathered by the same verb.
  ~~|
  ~(:item it | if (atomKinds | has (item | type)) ~([it]) ~(partsOf | get /parts | map ~atomsOf | flat))

:any/placeKey
  |~~ The key an atom's place is read by, the keyword of its print, which
      tells `1` from `"1"`.
  ~~|
  ~(print | toKeyword)

:any/numberedWith
  |~~ The atoms numbered so far, `{:next … :pairs …}`, with one more. ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :atom |~~ The atom numbered next. ~~| /0
    | impl
        ~(:acc it
          | {:next (acc | get /next | add 1) :pairs (acc | get /pairs | append [atom (acc | get /next)])})

:any/intoShape
  |~~ The steps built so far, `{:numbered … :steps …}`, with the step of
      one value after them: the read of an atom's place in the set,
      which `:numbered` holds under the atom's key, or the step that
      builds a value from the steps of its parts.
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :element |~~ The value whose step comes next. ~~| /0
    | impl
        ~(:acc it
          | element
          | :item it
          | if (atomKinds | has (item | type))
              ~({:numbered (acc | get /numbered)
                 :steps (acc | get /steps | append ([::call{:name :get :modifiers [([(acc | get /numbered | query (item | placeKey) | last)] | toPath)]}] | tag ::quote | tag ::group))})
              ~(partsOf | :built it
                | built | get /parts | reduce {:numbered (acc | get /numbered) :steps []} ~(intoShape) | :inner it
                | {:numbered (acc | get /numbered) :steps (acc | get /steps | append (inner | get /steps | groupBefore (built | get /glue)))}))

:any/apart
  |~~ The atoms of the subject and its shape. ~~|
  ::fn
    | proves :takesAValueApart
        |~~ A vector of a string, a vector and a map comes apart into four
            atoms and its shape.
        ~~|
        ~(["x" [1 1] {:b :a}] | apart | eq {:atoms #[1 "x" :a :b] :shape ~([(get /1) [(get /0) (get /0)] ([[(get /3) (get /2)]] | indexBy ~(first) | map ~last)])})
    | impl
        ~(:held [it]
          | :atoms (held | map ~atomsOf | flat | tag ::set)
          | :numbered (atoms | reduce {:next 0 :pairs []} ~(numberedWith) | get /pairs | indexBy ~(first | placeKey))
          | {:atoms atoms :shape (held | reduce {:numbered numbered :steps []} ~(intoShape) | get /steps | tag ::quote)})

:any/rebuilt
  |~~ The value the shape of the subject builds from its atoms. ~~|
  ~(apart | :pieces it | pieces | get /atoms | apply (pieces | get /shape))
